# chad3 -- Chad's last intermezzo, just before goodnight.
# Copyright 2026 Corwin Brust; CC-BY-SA-4.0
#
# Chad is Corwin's own character: brief, confident, a little out of place,
# explaining nothing. This is where his line is meant to land, near C4's
# query language (the goodnight page names C4QL). Nobody explains it.
#
# For the writers only, not the page or the voices:
# - C4.md section 9, 2026-08-25: "Verb families ride in-flight toward the
#   taxonomy via C4 backward consing (rightmost token = the logical CAR; left
#   to MEANING-STOP, most often colon; CAPITALS drive taxonomy movement) under
#   the ASSY / C4QL / C4META stack." (c4/C4.md lines 258-260, sha256
#   358ce65c...9d42.)
# - facts/c-for-command, lines 26-33: "grab the rightmost token (the logical
#   CAR), advance left to MEANING-STOP (most often COLON ':'); hunks cascade
#   right-to-left, each hunk read left-to-right until something means 'all by
#   itself' ... C4QL traces implementation to surface linkage and gaps by
#   dynamics of meaning". His own hand, in the steering file it digests
#   (/f/claude/C4-STEERING-2026-08-25-c-for-command.md, line 49): "now try the
#   C4 backward consing by grabing one token from the right (our "logical
#   CAR") and then then advancing left until MEANING-STOP".
# - What the page shows: Chad reads the book's own name from the right end.
#   "Wheel" first, the thing it is; then "Ghost", which wheel. Spoke, the ghost
#   at the hub since spread 1, waves. The cover draws Ghost and wheel in two
#   colours. That is the whole telegraph. If he wants it a tiny bit louder,
#   one candidate is a single sentence on the goodnight fuller page citing the
#   C4.md line above; it is left off on purpose (his words: "DO NOT ensure we
#   dive the point home ... I will be the judge of that").
kind: intermezzo
title: Chad

== picture page ==
Oh! Chad is back, one last time.

He looks at the name on the book.
"Wheel," he says. "Ghost."

Spoke waves.

"Last word first. Every time."

And then he was gone.

